  OVERLAY EXAMPLE — user/plugins/disciplined-vibe-coding/templates/writing-plan.md.example

  This file shows the shape of an overlay override. It is documentation only:
  the updater ignores *.example files, and nothing reads this path.

  To activate: copy to the mirror path (drop the .example suffix) and edit:

      cp user/plugins/disciplined-vibe-coding/templates/writing-plan.md.example \
         user/plugins/disciplined-vibe-coding/templates/writing-plan.md

  From then on the user/ copy replaces
  plugins/disciplined-vibe-coding/templates/writing-plan.md at use time.
  Updates replace the shipped template and reapply your copy on top.
-->

# Plan — [milestone name]

Purpose: atomic tasks one builder can run without asking anything else.

## Steps

Purpose: each step names its file, output, and pass check.
1. Path: / Content: / Expected output: / Pass check (observable):
2. ...

## Files touched

Purpose: full list, so review can check blast radius.
-

## Test strategy

Purpose: what fails first, what proves it passes (`test-first`: RED, then GREEN).
-

## Example customization (delete or replace with your own)

Purpose: this section does not exist in the shipped template. It is here to
show what an overlay change looks like — extra sections, tightened wording,
project-specific checklists. Keep what earns its keep; delete the rest.

## Timebox

Purpose: wall-clock budget for this milestone, so a stuck plan surfaces early.
Budget:
What gets cut if the budget runs out:

## Verify criteria

Purpose: the exact re-runnable checks `verify` will run.

## Rollback

Purpose: how to undo this plan if it goes wrong. Skip only if fully reversible.
-

## Commit message draft

Purpose: `type: concise subject`, ready at plan time.
